<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45716" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suāsĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		suadeo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a counselling</i>, <i>advice</i>, <i>exhortation</i>, <i>suasion</i>, <i>persuasion.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep.
				95, 65</span></i>.—<i>Plur.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omni suasionum admonitionumque genere utens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 10, 19, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In publicists'
			lang., <i>a recommending</i>, <i>advocacy</i> of a proposed law: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suasio legis Serviliae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Clu. 51, 140</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			rhetoric, <i>the suasory species of eloquence</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Or. 11, 37</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praecepta dare de suasionibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					de Or. 2, 81, 333</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
